     "text": "def get_common_elements(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list of elements that are common to both input lists.\n    \n    This function utilizes Python's set data structure to efficiently find\n    the intersection of two lists. The use of sets ensures that the operation\n    is performed in O(n) time complexity, where n is the size of the larger list.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    list1 (list): The first input list.\n    list2 (list): The second input list.\n    \n    Returns:\n    list: A list containing the common elements between list1 and list2.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert both lists to sets to leverage set operations\n    set1 = set(list1)\n    set2 = set(list2)\n    \n    # Find the intersection of the two sets\n    common_elements = set1 & set2\n    \n    # Convert the result back to a list and return\n    return list(common_elements)",
